WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.062
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.062 --> 00:00:09.180
This past summer,
I landed the internship of a lifetime.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:15.040
No, it wasn't that amazing business
development internship at AirBnB.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.800
Or that super sexy product
management role at Amazon.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.700
Or even that really cool secret project
at unnamed startup in self mode.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.970
It was an introjapat Costco.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:35.599
Yes, Costco wholesale, the place that
you might remember as a concrete jungle,

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:38.760
littered with oversized
red shopping carts.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.225
Or maybe the place that gives
away free food samples and

00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:45.390
is featured in Fresh Off the Boat
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.085
&gt;&gt; Or maybe you just remember it as this.

00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:50.686
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:00:50.686 --> 00:00:53.282
&gt;&gt; And you might be thinking to yourself,

00:00:53.282 --> 00:00:57.530
why would a former McKinsey consultant,
former VC investor And

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:02.450
current student at a business school
in the heart of Silicon Valley.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:04.979
Want to move to Issaquah,
Washington to work for a large and

00:01:04.979 --> 00:01:06.405
old school company like Costco?

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.798
Well as it turns out, most of us in this

00:01:10.798 --> 00:01:15.680
room have been chasing the next
sexy startup, the next big unicorn.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:21.110
But what about the companies that have
endured and existed for years on end?

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:24.905
I like to think of these as
the rhinos of the business world.

00:01:24.905 --> 00:01:25.840
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.652
&gt;&gt; They're definitely not sexy,

00:01:27.652 --> 00:01:31.220
they certainly have more wrinkles,
they're slower moving.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.406
They're more methodical but
they have have thicker skin,

00:01:35.406 --> 00:01:37.920
greater strength and more wisdom.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.780
And they may just be a little bit more
real then their mythological counterparts.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.510
Indeed, my summer opened my eyes to
just how wonderful these rhinos can be.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:54.049
The lessons I learned in humility,
in entrepreneurship and

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:57.520
in impact,
are ones that I will never forget.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.400
Lesson number one, working for
a rhino is humbling.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.541
My alarm clock at blared
at 3:15 in the morning,

00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:07.930
I rolled over, I hit the snooze button.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:09.329
And I thought to my self,

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:13.070
[SOUND] I could definitely use at
least a couple more hours of sleep.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:19.090
How could I possibly be this tired when
it was only my second day on the job.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:23.188
I made it outta bed, clocked into the
warehouse right at four in the morning,

00:02:23.188 --> 00:02:26.550
grabbed a pallet jack,
and reported for duty.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:30.344
Over the course of that morning my
hands got sore from moving what

00:02:30.344 --> 00:02:34.920
seemed like endless amounts of Campbell's
soup from one palate to the next.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.908
My back started to ache
as I swept the floors,

00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:43.350
making sure that our isles were showtime
ready for opening at 10 in the morning.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:51.190
It was the hardest work I had ever down,
and yet it only paid $20 an hour.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.110
I often thought to myself,
what am I doing here?

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.255
I couldn't help but
compare myself to my peers,

00:02:58.255 --> 00:03:02.410
who I imagined sitting at a desk
building fancy models in Excel.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.555
Or creating beautiful Powerpoint
presentations filled with interesting

00:03:06.555 --> 00:03:08.110
strategies.

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:12.940
And yet here I was, I had a hard time
seeing the value of sweeping floors.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.110
Or ringing customers up at the cash
registers and of making food in the deli.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.060
But then I met Joe.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:23.310
Joe had been with the company for
the last 12 years.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:25.920
You couldn't miss him with
the six foot two stature.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.370
His baggy sweatpants and
a backwards Raiders cap on at all times.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.968
You always knew that he was on shift
because you could hear his hip-hop and

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:37.930
rap music blasting from his
radio at 4:30 in the morning.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.657
And as I got to know him, I learned that
Joe didn't really know what he wanted to

00:03:41.657 --> 00:03:44.040
do with this life, but
he loved his job at Costco.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.638
He told me, the company's been
really good to me, it rewards me for

00:03:47.638 --> 00:03:50.630
something I'm actually pretty good at.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:55.100
So maybe one day, I'll apply to be
a supervisor, and I'll earn my red vest.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:59.320
And then maybe eventually,
I could be a manager.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:02.667
Joe's story was just one of
the many I heard this summer,

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:07.551
that reminded me that my fellow warehouse
workers were each trying to achieve their

00:04:07.551 --> 00:04:09.660
own version of the American dream.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.249
They might not have gone to the same
schools as us, or worked for

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:15.410
the same companies as us.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:20.400
But they too had an ambition to create
a life of meaning for themselves.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.383
Whether it was Nicki's love of her 4 AM
shift that enabled her to pick up her

00:04:24.383 --> 00:04:25.720
daughter after school.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:31.090
Or Alex's drive and determination
to work his way through college.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:38.230
They were all incredibly hardworking,
dedicated and damn good at their jobs.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.960
Now that's pretty humbling.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.590
Lesson number two,
you can be entrepreneurial and at a rhino.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.244
I remember I was out of breath
because I had been sprinting across

00:04:49.244 --> 00:04:52.640
150,000 square feet of
concrete warehouse floor.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.830
A customer had asked me if we still had
the sleep science mattress in stock.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.462
In pursuit of her question,

00:04:59.462 --> 00:05:03.610
I first ran over to the supervisor
to ask her if she knew.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.330
And then I ran over to the stocker who
typically worked the furniture department.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:11.679
And then finally I ran back to
the office to check our AS400 system,

00:05:11.679 --> 00:05:14.590
only to come up with the lousy answer.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:18.027
I'm so sorry ma'am our system
shows that we have one, but

00:05:18.027 --> 00:05:19.650
we don't know where it is.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.009
And I thought to myself,

00:05:22.009 --> 00:05:25.190
there must be a better way to
get this kind of information.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.023
And so I embarked on a journey
to build them a mobile app,

00:05:28.023 --> 00:05:31.899
that would let them see real-time
inventory levels right on their phones.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:36.289
Now let's not get carried away here,
I am by no means a coder but

00:05:36.289 --> 00:05:38.120
I'm pretty good at using Google.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:43.625
And so I hacked together what we might
generously call a minimum viable product.

00:05:43.625 --> 00:05:44.730
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.917
&gt;&gt; When I showed Tyler the merchandising

00:05:46.917 --> 00:05:48.836
manager the app, he was stoked.

00:05:48.836 --> 00:05:54.000
He asked if we could augment it,
add more data to it, show more dashboards.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:59.068
And pretty soon I had a bunch of team
members come up to me to ask me how to

00:05:59.068 --> 00:06:01.240
download it and if they could use it.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:04.155
So I identified a customer pinpoint,

00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:08.618
I designed a customer centric solution,
I built an MVP and

00:06:08.618 --> 00:06:11.785
I pivoted on that product.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:06:11.785 --> 00:06:15.150
&gt;&gt; And no, I wasn't working for a unicorn.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:18.285
Who says you have to work at one
to be an entrepreneur anyways?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.280
Lesson number three?

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.750
Rhinos shape communities.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.175
You've probably never heard of
a town called Fremont, Nebraska, but

00:06:28.175 --> 00:06:30.060
it's about an hour outside of Omaha.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.339
We were there visiting
Costco's construction site for

00:06:33.339 --> 00:06:36.977
their poultry processing plant
that had just broken ground.

00:06:36.977 --> 00:06:39.024
Freemont is pretty desolate,

00:06:39.024 --> 00:06:43.442
has one main street with a couple
of stop lights that hang on a wire.

00:06:43.442 --> 00:06:46.687
A few mom-and-pop shops,
one bar in town for all the locals.

00:06:46.687 --> 00:06:50.356
The only restaurant I recognized
was a Buffalo Wild Wings.

00:06:50.356 --> 00:06:54.815
Over the course of a three-night trip,
we eat there twice.

00:06:54.815 --> 00:06:56.120
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.711
&gt;&gt; And I remember sitting in

00:06:57.711 --> 00:07:00.220
the trailer on the construction site.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:03.144
And I was talking to Jonathan,
the plant manager and

00:07:03.144 --> 00:07:05.280
he was explaining to me the org chart.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.690
And I was shocked at the team
size they were proposing.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:14.990
As of April 2019, this plant would
create 800 new jobs in Freemont alone.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.430
I was stunned.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:18.850
I knew that rhinos had impact.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:23.759
Whether it was Costco's title as
the largest organic retailer in the US or

00:07:23.759 --> 00:07:27.020
the largest seller of USDA
choice in prime beef.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:28.637
I knew they were big, but

00:07:28.637 --> 00:07:34.540
what I hadn't fully realized is just
how much they impact local communities.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:38.141
They create employment, they create
opportunity, they create an economy.

00:07:39.382 --> 00:07:43.276
A few weeks ago, a CEO of a rhino
came to the GSP and asked us.

00:07:43.276 --> 00:07:47.579
Don't you want to do something
more than just sell ad space?

00:07:47.579 --> 00:07:50.353
Now maybe that's exactly
what you want to do or

00:07:50.353 --> 00:07:53.571
it's been your life's
passion to start a company.

00:07:53.571 --> 00:07:58.030
To be a management consultant,
to join a big tech firm.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:02.562
I'm not suggesting you shouldn't, but
what I am suggesting is that you take

00:08:02.562 --> 00:08:06.760
a moment to consider what you might
want to be able to achieve at a rhino.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:12.565
They're not for the faint of heart,
they don't offer free-flowing food or

00:08:12.565 --> 00:08:15.440
nap pods, Starwood points or
shuttle buses.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:22.040
But they do offer a platform for humility,
for entrepreneurship and impact.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:26.806
So while you're dreaming of what it might
be like to work at the next big unicorn

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:31.810
that has yet to exist, don't forget about
their long lost cousins, the rhinos.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:35.273
I'm excited to announce that I
will be rejoining Costco for

00:08:35.273 --> 00:08:39.090
their very official MBA rotational
program starting next fall.

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:42.630
And of one.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.036
&gt;&gt; Don't get me wrong,

00:08:44.036 --> 00:08:48.643
it terrifies me that I'm not joining
a rocket ship or the big three, or

00:08:48.643 --> 00:08:50.590
fund to funds.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.680
I'm scared that I'm zagging when everyone
else around us seems to be zigging.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:59.380
But I know that for
me joining a rhino is my best possible

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:04.286
opportunity to change lives,
change organizations and

00:09:04.286 --> 00:09:09.478
change the world.
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:09:09.478 --> 00:09:13.009
[MUSIC]

